  "geometryBasis": "The named mosque, its qibla alignment and adjacent tomb use native map controls. The Qualla plate and the 2004 architectural survey establish the 30.50 by 19.70 metre interior and six 9 metre diameter domes.",
  "sectionBasis": "The exact Qualla plate 24c is a measured historic plan with two sections. The drawing fixes the double gallery, sectional spacing, approximate spring 17.5 m and apex 22.5 m, and minaret height about 39.5 m. The Istanbul survey documents lead roofing, pale cut limestone, brick vaulting and the southern weight towers.",
  "limitations": [
    "The model represents the standing mosque galleries, prayer hall and extant türbe. Former medrese and dervish lodge wings are outside the represented period.",
    "The long span and reference sections produce estimated external dimensions. Portico paving, tomb eaves and sill heights follow approximate terrain grades.",
    "Mortar details, timber joinery, finial ornament and individual stone panels are generalized. Interior tilework and furniture are outside the model scope."
  ],
